+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"build","node_id":"F2","attempt":3,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/build/F2/verdicts/A2-reviewer.json R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6; docs/trace/build/F2/verdicts/A2-security.json P2 note (cancellationToken query key)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PolicyResponseAssert.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Builders/PolicyBuilder.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs:37 passes a literal false for hasClaims at green, under the stub-step comment at :23 ('canned until F3 supplies the data'). The data is supplied today: Policy.HasClaims (src/Uinsure.Policies.Domain/Policies/Policy.cs:33) is stored (src/Uinsure.Policies.Persistence/PolicyRepository.cs:70) and restored (src/Uinsure.Policies.Persistence/PolicyRecordMapper.cs:21). GET-1 says 'Returns the policy', and requirements.md:112 lists HasClaims as a Policy field. Cause (classification: tests): the t1 oracle cannot tell the canned value from the stored one. PolicyResponseAssert.cs:47 only ever expects false, and the Api.Tests PolicyBuilder passes a literal false to Policy.Restore at PolicyBuilder.cs:54, with no way to override it. A grep of tests/ finds no test anywhere that stores or expects true. So 'whole acceptance suite green' (build.dag.yaml:218, t8) was met with the stub constant still in place. At HEAD no endpoint can make HasClaims true (COULD-2: false at sale; claims arrive in F3), so the defect shows only on a seeded policy. That is why the red test must seed one. Hypothesis inv-001: neither disproof condition holds. hasClaims has a stored source at the reviewed head, and no test seeds true. The brief leg is unverified: the t2/t8 dispatch prompts are not in the trace or packet. The trail shows three things. The :23 comment was written at the t2 stub (packet/diff.patch:198; A1 cited the same :32/:33 line numbers at 305789d). The t8 title carves out nothing ('response contract per api-contract'). The t8 builder read only Terms/CurrentTerm and PolicyDetails before editing (activity.jsonl:196), never HasClaims. So the stub's own comment acted as scope at green; whether a brief said so cannot be shown from this evidence. The hypothesis explains R1 and A1 only, not R2-R6. Recurrence: same class as A1 I1/I2 (a canned value equal to every value the tests expect), a new field and line, so a new fingerprint. A1's route fixed two constants (aee97ab, PolicyMappings.cs only; loop.jsonl:7) and did not dispatch the tester (loop.jsonl:6). That treated the symptom. gate.stub counts failing tests, not whether each canned member has an assertion that can fail. At attempt 2's gate.stub, the 21 rows failed on status and term number while hasClaims=false still matched every expectation, so nothing exposed it. Once fixed, the :23 comment also becomes partly untrue (see I2). Fix direction: first a red test that reads back a stored true; then map the policy's stored value, and keep only refunds, claims and cancellation canned.","fingerprint":"GET-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PolicyResponseAssert.cs|has-claims-never-varied","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a policy seeded through the app's IPolicyRepository with HasClaims stored true (PolicyBuilder gains a way to set it instead of the literal false), When GET /policies/{reference} is called, Then hasClaims reads back true and the rest of the read-back matches the seed; the existing sold-policy rows keep expecting false (RetrieveResponseShapeTests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyResponse.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyResponse.cs:3-4 says status and currentTermNumber are 'canned for now (stub step)'. At HEAD both are real: PolicyMappings.cs:32 maps details.Status, and :33 maps the current term's index. Cause (classification: code): the comment was written at the t2 stub (packet/diff.patch:242-243). Green changed only PolicyMappings.cs, TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs, RejectUnknownQueryParametersFilter.cs and Program.cs (loop.jsonl:12). The t9 refactor changed only the converter's comment (loop.jsonl:14). Nobody re-read the stub-step comments in the other file the stub touched. This is the same lifecycle gap as I1, where stub-step text survived into green. But the defect is a false comment, not a behaviour, so it is a separate finding. Not a recurrence of A1. Fix direction: make the PolicyResponse header say what is true at HEAD, and keep the 'still canned' list in one place (PolicyMappings.cs:23), updated once I1 lands.","fingerprint":"GET-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyResponse.cs|stale-stub-comment","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"A source comment has no runtime behaviour, so no test can observe whether it is true; it is checked at refactor and review."},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Program.cs","tests/postman/Uinsure.Policies.postman_collection.json"],"root_cause":"Symptom: every decimal the API writes passes through src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs:17, registered globally at Program.cs (packet/diff.patch:364). It writes value.ToString('F2'), which rounds any value with more than 2 dp. Cause (classification: code): t8 asked for money 'formatted to exactly 2 dp in every response' (build.dag.yaml:218). The builder chose a format that both pads and rounds, where padding alone was asked for. The 'no more than 2 dp reaches it' invariant lives only in the comment at lines 7-10, and the code does not enforce it. CLAUDE.md says to round money only through Money.Round. No Money type exists in src/ at HEAD (grep finds none; 803c898 corrected a comment that cited it, loop.jsonl:14). So this converter is the only code that rounds at all. When F3 adds refunds (CANCEL-6), it would hide a missing or wrong Money.Round from every Api test. The evidence gap is real but secondary: the problem-echo text change (-1e27 now written with .00) is evidenced only by gate.run (loop.jsonl:13). The Postman decimal.MinValue check uses include('\"amount\":-79228162514264337593543950335') (postman collection :3486), a prefix match that passes with or without '.00'. Not a recurrence. Fix direction: make writing unable to change a value. Either pad the scale only, or reject a value with more than 2 dp loudly. David rules which one. Then pin the echo text exactly.","fingerprint":"GET-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs|f2-format-rounds","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the app's configured JSON options, When a response carrying a decimal with more than 2 dp (for example 0.125) is written, Then the written value is not silently rounded (it is either written exactly or rejected, per David's ruling), and the SELL-7 problem echo of -1e27 is pinned to its exact text (PolicyMoneyFormatTests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I4","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Filters/RejectUnknownQueryParametersFilter.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveNotFoundTests.cs"],"root_cause":"This finding explicitly covers both reviewer R4 and the security P2 note (cancellationToken query key accepted and ignored). They share one cause, stated here rather than merged silently. Symptom: ?reference= and ?cancellationToken= on GET, and ?request= on POST, pass without a 400. Cause (classification: code): src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Filters/RejectUnknownQueryParametersFilter.cs:11 builds the known-key set from every ActionDescriptor parameter name, whatever its binding source. PoliciesController.cs:29 declares Get(string reference, CancellationToken cancellationToken): the first is bound from the route, the second is a special parameter. PoliciesController.cs:16 declares Sell(SellPolicyRequest request, ...), and request is bound from the body. None of these is a query key, but all are counted as one. The rule violated: requirements.md:124 ('an unknown query parameter ... return 400'); the architecture contract also says 'an unbound query key (case-insensitive) gives errors[key]'. The only test sends ?colour=red (RetrieveNotFoundTests.cs:75), a key that matches no parameter at all, so it cannot expose this. Security rated it harmless (no security effect); the reviewer rated it P2 for correctness. Not a recurrence. Fix direction: count as known only the parameters that are actually bound from the query string.","fingerprint":"GET-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Filters/RejectUnknownQueryParametersFilter.cs|known-keys-ignore-binding-source","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a sold policy, When GET /policies/{reference}?reference=X and, separately, GET /policies/{reference}?cancellationToken=1 are sent, Then each answers 400 with errors[reference] or errors[cancellationToken] and no ruleId; and When POST /policies?request=x is sent with a valid body, Then it answers 400 with errors[request] (RetrieveNotFoundTests, SellShapeTests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I5","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveCurrentTermTests.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: Unpaid_second_term_reads_back_with_no_payment_reference_and_no_payment (tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveCurrentTermTests.cs:75-95) never asserts status. Every other row in the class asserts a status literal (:39, :49, and the term-2 and Expired rows). Cause (classification: tests): the row's read-back calls ReadsBackTheSeededPolicy (:90), AssertTerms, AssertPayment and ShowsCurrentTerm (:94). None of them checks status, so the read-back is not full, as the tdd-outside-in skill requires for every field the response carries. The row is stub-proof only through currentTermNumber. Recurrence: this is not A1 I2's cause line, which was the canned term number at PolicyMappings.cs:33 and has since been fixed. It is the gap A1 I2 itself named: 'Unpaid_second_term has no status assertion ... only the term number can fail it' (findings/A1.md). A1's route kept the fix code-only and did not dispatch the tester (loop.jsonl:6). So the named test gap was never closed, and the reviewer raised it again. New fingerprint, because the cause sits in a different file. Fix direction: add the row's expected status literal (Active, with today 2026-10-17 inside term 1) so that the row depends on two derived values.","fingerprint":"GET-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveCurrentTermTests.cs|unpaid-row-no-status","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the unpaid-second-term policy seeded with term 1 paid and term 2 unpaid, and today 2026-10-17 inside term 1, When GET /policies/GET1-UNPAID-T2 is called, Then status is Active as well as currentTermNumber 1 and the existing term and payment assertions (RetrieveCurrentTermTests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I6","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Services.Tests/PolicyServiceGetDetailsTests.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Services/PolicyService.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: no Services test covers the not-found branch of PolicyService.Get. src/Uinsure.Policies.Services/PolicyService.cs:57-63 builds that violation: RuleIds.Get1, ViolationKind.NotFound, detail 'No policy with reference ...', and a reference extension. Every test in tests/Uinsure.Policies.Services.Tests/PolicyServiceGetDetailsTests.cs:29-102 stores a policy first. Its Found helper asserts IsSuccess (:114). Cause (classification: tests, carried by an orchestrator decision): t6 ran as 'trait + gap-fill' under David's t4 ruling. It traited the six F1b found-path tests and changed no assertions. The orchestrator recorded the gap in the gate.green receipt and did not close it ('Gap noted, not closed: no Services test for the GET-1 not-found result', loop.jsonl:10). The gap-fill half of the ruling was therefore not carried out for this branch. The branch is proven only over HTTP, by RetrieveNotFoundTests. Not a recurrence. Fix direction: add a Services-level test for the not-found result, so that GET-1's failure row is proven at the layer that builds it.","fingerprint":"GET-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Services.Tests/PolicyServiceGetDetailsTests.cs|no-not-found-unit-test","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given an empty RecordingPolicyRepository, When PolicyService.Get is called for reference GET1-SVC-NONE, Then the result fails with exactly one violation whose RuleId is GET-1, Kind is NotFound, detail is 'No policy with reference 'GET1-SVC-NONE'.' and reference extension is GET1-SVC-NONE (PolicyServiceGetDetailsTests)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["A1: attempt 1, gate.stub FAIL at 305789d. 12 of 25 GET-1 tests passed because the canned status Active (I1) and the canned currentTermNumber 1 (I2) matched expected values. Fixed in aee97ab by canning Cancelled and 0, touching PolicyMappings.cs only. Tester not dispatched (loop.jsonl:6). That route fixed two constants, not the class: the canned hasClaims=false still matched every expectation (now I1), and the unpaid row's missing status assertion that A1 I2 named was left open (now I5).","A2: attempt 2, reviewer FAIL at 8ea8f60 (pre-rebase id; the code is identical after the rebase onto c4b6231). R1 P1: hasClaims hard-coded false though stored. R2-R6 P2. Security PASS with a P2 note on the cancellationToken query key (covered by I4). The A2 code fingerprints (I2-I4, I6) are new; I1 is the A1 class on a new field; I5 is the A1 I2 gap left open."]}
